1
00:00:00,281 --> 00:00:02,472
Last video ended on this curve: e to

2
00:00:02,493 --> 00:00:03,960
the x, over x plus one.

3
00:00:04,603 --> 00:00:06,569
At x equals minus one, the bottom is

4
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:09,379
zero, and you can't divide by zero, so

5
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:10,382
there's no curve there.

6
00:00:11,166 --> 00:00:13,533
A fraction like this works like average speed,

7
00:00:13,915 --> 00:00:16,443
distance over time, and you can't average over

8
00:00:16,504 --> 00:00:17,225
zero time.

9
00:00:18,252 --> 00:00:20,288
Now the slope at x equals zero.

10
00:00:20,953 --> 00:00:21,534
A quick guess:

11
00:00:22,057 --> 00:00:23,040
divide the derivatives.

12
00:00:23,744 --> 00:00:25,488
The top's derivative is e to the x,

13
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:26,953
and the bottom's is one,

14
00:00:27,456 --> 00:00:29,101
so the guess gives a slope of one

15
00:00:29,242 --> 00:00:30,244
at x equals zero.

16
00:00:30,788 --> 00:00:32,200
But the tangent there is flat.

17
00:00:33,067 --> 00:00:35,533
So how do we really differentiate a quotient,

18
00:00:35,855 --> 00:00:37,378
and keep track of where it's defined?

19
00:00:38,009 --> 00:00:39,284
Let's take that road trip.

20
00:00:39,829 --> 00:00:42,134
Your average speed is the distance so far,

21
00:00:42,275 --> 00:00:43,337
over the time so far.

22
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:46,069
After one hour you've gone a hundred kilometres,

23
00:00:46,351 --> 00:00:48,078
so your average is a hundred kilometres an

24
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:48,259
hour.

25
00:00:48,903 --> 00:00:51,433
Keep driving, and more distance pushes the average

26
00:00:51,635 --> 00:00:53,562
up, but more time pulls it down.

27
00:00:54,285 --> 00:00:56,129
Drive at a hundred and twenty, faster than

28
00:00:56,150 --> 00:00:58,875
your average, and the push wins: the average

29
00:00:58,936 --> 00:00:59,256
rises.

30
00:00:59,938 --> 00:01:02,390
Slow to sixty for roadworks, and the pull

31
00:01:02,431 --> 00:01:03,556
wins: it falls.

32
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,654
Now hold exactly a hundred, your average, and

33
00:01:07,675 --> 00:01:09,301
the two cancel, so it stays flat.

34
00:01:09,664 --> 00:01:11,170
That's our flat tangent.

35
00:01:11,694 --> 00:01:13,778
Dividing the two rates only gives your speed

36
00:01:13,979 --> 00:01:16,564
right now, not how fast the average is

37
00:01:16,606 --> 00:01:16,945
changing.

38
00:01:17,489 --> 00:01:19,022
Think about what each part does.

39
00:01:19,688 --> 00:01:20,993
For this positive fraction,

40
00:01:21,516 --> 00:01:24,628
top growth pushes up and bottom growth pulls

41
00:01:24,689 --> 00:01:24,969
down.

42
00:01:25,713 --> 00:01:27,858
At x equals zero, the top, e to

43
00:01:27,899 --> 00:01:29,603
the x, is growing at a rate of

44
00:01:29,845 --> 00:01:32,251
one, and that pushes y up at a

45
00:01:32,292 --> 00:01:32,713
rate of one.

46
00:01:33,356 --> 00:01:36,024
The bottom, x plus one, is also growing

47
00:01:36,086 --> 00:01:37,670
at a rate of one, and that pulls

48
00:01:37,892 --> 00:01:39,296
y down at a rate of one.

49
00:01:39,980 --> 00:01:41,986
The push and the pull cancel, so the

50
00:01:42,027 --> 00:01:42,788
slope is zero.

51
00:01:43,552 --> 00:01:45,637
At x equals one, the push is about

52
00:01:45,798 --> 00:01:47,903
one point three six, and the pull is

53
00:01:47,924 --> 00:01:48,966
about point six eight,

54
00:01:49,489 --> 00:01:51,474
so the slope is about point six eight.

55
00:01:52,057 --> 00:01:54,183
That pull is the minus sign in the

56
00:01:54,204 --> 00:01:54,745
quotient rule.

57
00:01:55,202 --> 00:01:56,998
You met the quotient rule in Year 11.

58
00:01:57,745 --> 00:01:59,058
Here's why it has that shape.

59
00:01:59,803 --> 00:02:02,071
Dividing by g is the same as multiplying

60
00:02:02,112 --> 00:02:04,701
by one over g, so use last video's

61
00:02:04,763 --> 00:02:05,324
product rule.

62
00:02:05,967 --> 00:02:08,274
The top's turn is f prime, times one

63
00:02:08,334 --> 00:02:08,715
over g.

64
00:02:09,397 --> 00:02:11,301
For the bottom's turn, the chain rule says

65
00:02:11,481 --> 00:02:14,347
one over g has derivative minus g prime,

66
00:02:14,467 --> 00:02:15,208
over g squared.

67
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:17,856
So that turn is minus f g prime,

68
00:02:17,958 --> 00:02:18,659
over g squared.

69
00:02:19,463 --> 00:02:21,489
Put both turns over g squared, and you

70
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:23,878
get f prime g, minus f g prime,

71
00:02:24,361 --> 00:02:25,323
all over g squared.

72
00:02:26,087 --> 00:02:28,495
The top's derivative comes first, the minus is

73
00:02:28,516 --> 00:02:30,462
the bottom's pull, and the whole bottom is

74
00:02:30,523 --> 00:02:30,944
squared.

75
00:02:31,746 --> 00:02:32,747
Check our curve at zero:

76
00:02:33,470 --> 00:02:34,471
f prime g is one,

77
00:02:35,013 --> 00:02:36,755
f g prime is one, so the top

78
00:02:36,856 --> 00:02:38,658
is one minus one, which is zero.

79
00:02:39,230 --> 00:02:40,343
Let's use it on our curve.

80
00:02:40,969 --> 00:02:44,456
Before differentiating, write where it's defined: x can't

81
00:02:44,517 --> 00:02:45,218
be minus one.

82
00:02:45,964 --> 00:02:46,532
Now the parts.

83
00:02:47,383 --> 00:02:49,476
f is e to the x, and so

84
00:02:49,538 --> 00:02:50,161
is f prime.

85
00:02:50,705 --> 00:02:53,397
g is x plus one, so g prime

86
00:02:53,559 --> 00:02:54,000
is one.

87
00:02:54,744 --> 00:02:56,607
The top of the answer is e to

88
00:02:56,628 --> 00:02:59,774
the x times x plus one, minus e

89
00:02:59,815 --> 00:03:00,896
to the x times one.

90
00:03:01,598 --> 00:03:03,101
Take out e to the x, and the

91
00:03:03,142 --> 00:03:06,127
bracket becomes x plus one minus one, which

92
00:03:06,208 --> 00:03:06,909
is just x.

93
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:09,918
So d y by d x is x

94
00:03:10,119 --> 00:03:12,265
e to the x, over x plus one

95
00:03:12,326 --> 00:03:14,913
squared, for x not equal to minus one.

96
00:03:15,696 --> 00:03:18,263
At x equals zero, that's zero, the flat

97
00:03:18,344 --> 00:03:19,065
tangent we saw.

98
00:03:19,692 --> 00:03:20,504
Now a harder one.

99
00:03:20,868 --> 00:03:23,192
Differentiate y equals the natural log of x,

100
00:03:23,413 --> 00:03:25,757
over cos x, and find the gradient at

101
00:03:25,939 --> 00:03:26,559
x equals one.

102
00:03:27,504 --> 00:03:30,015
The outside operation is division, so it's the

103
00:03:30,076 --> 00:03:30,658
quotient rule.

104
00:03:31,402 --> 00:03:32,057
Domain first.

105
00:03:32,684 --> 00:03:35,068
The natural log needs x positive, and the

106
00:03:35,129 --> 00:03:37,774
bottom can't be zero, so cos x can't

107
00:03:37,815 --> 00:03:38,255
be zero.

108
00:03:39,084 --> 00:03:39,630
Now the parts.

109
00:03:40,318 --> 00:03:42,047
f is the natural log of x, so

110
00:03:42,209 --> 00:03:43,636
f prime is one over x.

111
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:46,630
g is cos x, so g prime is

112
00:03:46,772 --> 00:03:47,696
minus sine x.

113
00:03:48,621 --> 00:03:50,650
f prime g is cos x over x.

114
00:03:51,293 --> 00:03:53,779
Then minus f g prime is minus the

115
00:03:53,821 --> 00:03:56,227
natural log of x, times minus sine x,

116
00:03:56,609 --> 00:03:58,193
and the two minus signs make a plus.

117
00:03:59,016 --> 00:04:00,822
All of that sits over cos squared x.

118
00:04:02,202 --> 00:04:04,199
Now put x equals one.

119
00:04:04,822 --> 00:04:07,148
The natural log of one is zero, so

120
00:04:07,188 --> 00:04:08,853
the second term on top vanishes.

121
00:04:09,474 --> 00:04:11,240
That's the bottom's pull disappearing:

122
00:04:11,782 --> 00:04:13,568
when the top is zero, a change in

123
00:04:13,609 --> 00:04:15,315
the bottom can't move the fraction.

124
00:04:16,137 --> 00:04:19,189
What's left is cos one, over cos squared

125
00:04:19,330 --> 00:04:21,338
one, which is one over cos one.

126
00:04:22,181 --> 00:04:24,906
With x in radians, that's about one point

127
00:04:25,027 --> 00:04:25,667
eight five,

128
00:04:26,169 --> 00:04:28,212
and the tangent at the point one, zero

129
00:04:28,313 --> 00:04:28,713
agrees.

130
00:04:29,616 --> 00:04:31,843
Get the order backwards, and you'd get minus

131
00:04:31,984 --> 00:04:34,633
one point eight five, a falling tangent, but

132
00:04:34,654 --> 00:04:35,677
the curve is rising there.

133
00:04:36,441 --> 00:04:38,673
And in degrees you'd get about one, which

134
00:04:38,714 --> 00:04:39,236
is also wrong.

135
00:04:40,002 --> 00:04:41,616
One more habit, for simplifying.

136
00:04:42,382 --> 00:04:46,162
Differentiate y equals sine x, over x squared.

137
00:04:46,785 --> 00:04:48,913
The bottom can't be zero, so x can't

138
00:04:48,933 --> 00:04:49,294
be zero.

139
00:04:50,156 --> 00:04:53,021
The quotient rule gives x squared cos x,

140
00:04:53,542 --> 00:04:55,185
minus two x sine x,

141
00:04:55,686 --> 00:04:56,727
all over x to the four.

142
00:04:57,691 --> 00:04:59,517
Both terms on top share a factor of

143
00:04:59,718 --> 00:05:01,946
x, so take it out, and cancel it

144
00:05:02,007 --> 00:05:03,311
with one x from the bottom.

145
00:05:03,994 --> 00:05:06,483
That's allowed only because x isn't zero.

146
00:05:07,204 --> 00:05:10,169
So the answer is x cos x, minus

147
00:05:10,309 --> 00:05:10,990
two sine x,

148
00:05:11,511 --> 00:05:12,353
over x cubed,

149
00:05:12,954 --> 00:05:14,957
and it still comes with x not equal

150
00:05:14,997 --> 00:05:15,378
to zero.

151
00:05:16,161 --> 00:05:18,311
Cancelling a factor never gives back a point

152
00:05:18,331 --> 00:05:19,978
the original function didn't have.

153
00:05:20,569 --> 00:05:22,084
Here's the classic way to remember it.

154
00:05:22,689 --> 00:05:25,060
Low dee high, minus high dee low,

155
00:05:25,644 --> 00:05:26,527
over low squared.

156
00:05:27,372 --> 00:05:29,120
High is the top, and low is the

157
00:05:29,141 --> 00:05:29,381
bottom.

158
00:05:30,265 --> 00:05:32,308
Low dee high means the bottom times the

159
00:05:32,329 --> 00:05:33,431
derivative of the top,

160
00:05:34,013 --> 00:05:35,936
which is the same as f prime g.

161
00:05:36,779 --> 00:05:39,445
Saying low first keeps the order right, and

162
00:05:39,466 --> 00:05:41,130
the minus is the bottom's pull.

163
00:05:41,832 --> 00:05:44,277
And unlike a product, the order matters here:

164
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:47,305
reversing the terms negates the derivative.

165
00:05:50,053 --> 00:05:50,440
Your turn.

166
00:05:51,209 --> 00:05:54,177
Differentiate y equals e to the x, over

167
00:05:54,419 --> 00:05:56,564
x plus two, and state any value of

168
00:05:56,686 --> 00:05:58,089
x that must be excluded.

169
00:05:58,732 --> 00:05:59,557
Pause here to answer.

170
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:11,643
Domain first:

171
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:13,550
x can't be minus two.

172
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:15,986
f prime is e to the x, and

173
00:06:16,026 --> 00:06:16,994
g prime is one.

174
00:06:17,375 --> 00:06:19,016
So the top is e to the x

175
00:06:19,096 --> 00:06:21,438
times x plus two, minus e to the

176
00:06:21,658 --> 00:06:21,778
x,

177
00:06:22,419 --> 00:06:24,180
which factors to e to the x, times

178
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,061
x plus one.

179
00:06:25,781 --> 00:06:27,663
So d y by d x is e

180
00:06:27,683 --> 00:06:29,844
to the x times x plus one, over

181
00:06:29,964 --> 00:06:32,306
x plus two squared, for x not equal

182
00:06:32,326 --> 00:06:32,927
to minus two.

183
00:06:33,769 --> 00:06:35,173
Start with high dee low instead,

184
00:06:35,676 --> 00:06:36,799
and you negate the derivative.

185
00:06:38,510 --> 00:06:38,873
Last one.

186
00:06:39,599 --> 00:06:42,388
Find the gradient of the curve y equals

187
00:06:42,509 --> 00:06:44,575
the natural log of x, over x,

188
00:06:45,158 --> 00:06:46,362
at x equals e.

189
00:06:47,233 --> 00:06:48,021
Pause here to answer.

190
00:06:58,755 --> 00:07:01,205
For positive x, f prime is one over

191
00:07:01,427 --> 00:07:01,547
x,

192
00:07:02,090 --> 00:07:03,234
and g prime is one.

193
00:07:03,897 --> 00:07:06,138
The top is one over x times x,

194
00:07:06,599 --> 00:07:08,780
minus the natural log of x, so it's

195
00:07:08,981 --> 00:07:10,622
one minus the natural log of x.

196
00:07:11,203 --> 00:07:13,508
So d y by d x is one

197
00:07:13,729 --> 00:07:15,452
minus the natural log of x, over x

198
00:07:15,494 --> 00:07:15,813
squared.

199
00:07:16,657 --> 00:07:18,986
At x equals e, the natural log of

200
00:07:19,008 --> 00:07:21,458
e is one, so the gradient is zero.

201
00:07:22,101 --> 00:07:24,186
Dividing the derivatives would give one over e,

202
00:07:24,228 --> 00:07:25,912
but the tangent at e is flat.

203
00:07:27,700 --> 00:07:30,944
A quotient combines both turns, with the minus

204
00:07:31,024 --> 00:07:33,146
in the bottom's term, and keeps its domain.

205
00:07:34,132 --> 00:07:36,487
Next, we'll use the sign of a derivative.

206
00:07:37,289 --> 00:07:39,051
Here's the derivative of our first curve,

207
00:07:39,571 --> 00:07:41,633
x e to the x, over x plus

208
00:07:41,753 --> 00:07:42,334
one squared.

209
00:07:43,134 --> 00:07:44,996
Where is it positive, where is it negative,

210
00:07:45,417 --> 00:07:47,900
and what happens at x equals minus one?

